  "research.ultimatearmoury.thaumic_meshes.title": "Thaumic Meshes",
  "research.ultimatearmoury.thaumic_meshes.stage_0": "The Ex Deorum sieve keeps whatever its mesh cannot hold. Alchemical brass, thaumium and void metal take a thread finer than any metal I have woven before, but they have to be woven on top of the finest unobtainium mesh.",
  "research.ultimatearmoury.thaumic_meshes.stage_1": "The brass mesh is woven at the arcane workbench around an unobtainium mesh, with brass ingots and string, for 100 vis and 64 crystals of each of the six primals.<BR>The thaumium mesh and the void metal mesh are made in an infusion altar. The mesh of the tier below goes into the runic matrix, and the ingots and string go on the pedestals around it.<BR>Each of them sifts amber out of gravel and sand, and cinnabar out of crushed deepslate and crushed netherrack. The brass mesh gives up 30% of what the ground holds, the thaumium mesh 65%, and the void metal mesh all of it.",
  "research.ultimatearmoury.thaumic_hammers.title": "Thaumic Hammers",
  "research.ultimatearmoury.thaumic_hammers.stage_0": "A mesh is only half of a sieve. The same three metals make hammers that break the ground down before it reaches the mesh.",
  "research.ultimatearmoury.thaumic_hammers.stage_1": "The brass hammer is made at the arcane workbench around an unobtainium hammer, for 100 vis and 64 crystals of each primal. The thaumium and void metal hammers are infused at an altar around the hammer of the tier below.<BR>Nine hammers of one metal press into a compressed hammer at the arcane workbench, which asks for the same price again.",
  "research.ultimatearmoury.thaumic_heaters.title": "Thaumic Heaters",
  "research.ultimatearmoury.thaumic_heaters.stage_0": "Blocks of alchemical brass, thaumium and void metal hold heat far longer than stone does.",
  "research.ultimatearmoury.thaumic_heaters.stage_1": "Set under an Ex Deorum crucible, a block of brass keeps it hot, a block of thaumium keeps it hotter, and a block of void metal is the hottest heater I know of."
}
